From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: park the byte and pixel sources on an xo clock

The previous patch moves the byte and pixel RCGs back to the parent they
had at the first link-up before the PHY PLL goes off. When the bootloader
hands the panel over lit, that parent is the PLL itself and the restore
does nothing: on the KONKR Pocket FIT Elite both sources still named
dsi0_phy_pll_out_* through a whole rest.

Take an optional "xo" clock on the controller and park on that instead.
It is the RCGs' parent 0 (bi_tcxo), where the vendor driver parks them
before it switches the PLL off (dsi_display_set_clk_src(display, true)),
and both stock SM8750 device trees give the DSI controllers this clock.
Without the clock the recorded parent is used as before. A reparent that
fails is now reported.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -294,6 +294,7 @@
 int dsi_clk_init_6g_v2_9(struct msm_dsi_host *msm_host)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &msm_host->pdev->dev;
+	struct clk *xo;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = dsi_clk_init_6g_v2(msm_host);
@@ -320,6 +321,17 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(msm_host->dsi_pll_pixel_clk),
 				     "can't get dsi_pll_pixel clock\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * Where the two sources rest while the PHY PLL is off. Without it they
+	 * go back to the parent found at the first link-up, which is the PLL
+	 * itself when the bootloader left the panel lit.
+	 */
+	xo = devm_clk_get_optional(dev, "xo");
+	if (IS_ERR(xo))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(xo), "can't get xo clock\n");
+	msm_host->byte_src_parent = xo;
+	msm_host->pixel_src_parent = xo;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -2633,10 +2645,12 @@
 
 	pinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state(&msm_host->pdev->dev);
 
-	if (msm_host->byte_src_parent)
-		clk_set_parent(msm_host->byte_src_clk, msm_host->byte_src_parent);
-	if (msm_host->pixel_src_parent)
-		clk_set_parent(msm_host->pixel_src_clk, msm_host->pixel_src_parent);
+	if (msm_host->byte_src_parent &&
+	    clk_set_parent(msm_host->byte_src_clk, msm_host->byte_src_parent))
+		dev_err(&msm_host->pdev->dev, "Failed to park byte_src\n");
+	if (msm_host->pixel_src_parent &&
+	    clk_set_parent(msm_host->pixel_src_clk, msm_host->pixel_src_parent))
+		dev_err(&msm_host->pdev->dev, "Failed to park pixel_src\n");
 
 	cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_disable(msm_host);
 	pm_runtime_put(&msm_host->pdev->dev);
